{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Spike7aParent",
    "description": "PLAN.md step 7a, the parent half: SPELLING A. The thin document that supplies everything `age_group_census.esm` leaves open — two `data_sources` entries, the two metaparameters that close its index sets, and the mount — and nothing else. It contains no arithmetic of its own beyond the one identity equation finding F21 forces.\n\nTHIS IS THE SHAPE PHASE 7 ASSUMES. The child declares `update: {kind: \"data\", source: \"spike_agecategory\"}` on three of its variables and declares neither key; both keys are declared HERE. If that resolves, then `moves-onroad.esm` can hold the whole domain's logic and bindings and a per-fixture document need only carry its `data_sources` and its runspec numbers, which is §7.1's premise.\n\nTHE PATH IS ABSOLUTE AND MACHINE-LOCAL, deliberately. The default database is not in this repository and must not be (it is 1.1 GB), so a `url_template` naming it cannot be repository-relative the way a snapshot path can. run-tests.sh SKIPS this stage when the directory is absent rather than failing, which is how the fixture stage already treats a missing snapshot corpus. Override with MOVESDB=/path.\n\nWHY THE ASSERTIONS ARE WHERE THEY ARE. The child's own tests run under this mount and assert the child's own names. This document adds one assertion of its own, on `parentTotalAge`, which is `AgeGroupCensus.totalAge` routed through a variable this model declares — the F21 workaround, and the only shape in which a mounting document can pin a mounted value at all. Both halves are needed: the child's tests prove the binding evaluates, and this one proves the value is reachable from the configuring document, which is where a fixture's canonical-output assertions will live.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "spike", "phase7", "run"]
  },

  "data_sources": {
    "spike_agecategory": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": { "url_template": "file:///scratch/ctessum/movesdb/movesdb20241112/AgeCategory.parquet" },
      "extent": { "metaparameter": "n_spike_agecategory" },
      "metadata": { "tags": ["default-db"], "note": "41 rows. The default database's agecategory table, unmodified.", "esio_format": "parquet" }
    },
    "spike_agegroup": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": { "url_template": "file:///scratch/ctessum/movesdb/movesdb20241112/AgeGroup.parquet" },
      "extent": { "metaparameter": "n_spike_agegroup" },
      "metadata": { "tags": ["default-db"], "note": "7 rows. The default database's agegroup table, unmodified.", "esio_format": "parquet" }
    }
  },

  "metaparameters": {
    "n_spike_agecategory": {
      "type": "integer", "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in agecategory. Runtime-discovered by `extent` (docs/esm-conventions.md §11), and the value that closes the child's `spike_agecategory_rows`."
    },
    "n_spike_agegroup": {
      "type": "integer", "default": 0,
      "description": "Rows in agegroup. Closes the child's `spike_agegroup_rows`."
    }
  },

  "models": {
    "AgeGroupCensus": { "ref": "./age_group_census.esm" },

    "Check": {
      "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12 },

      "variables": {
        "parentTotalAge": {
          "type": "unknown", "units": "1",
          "description": "The child's `totalAge`, routed through a variable this model declares because a scoped name is not assertable (finding F21). The identity equation is the cost of that finding, not a modelling choice."
        }
      },

      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "parentTotalAge",
          "rhs": { "op": "index", "args": ["AgeGroupCensus.totalAge"] }
        }
      ],

      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "the_configuring_document_can_read_the_mounted_result",
          "description": "820 again, but named by THIS model. The child's tests prove the parent-supplied binding evaluates; this proves the result crosses back up the mount into the document that configured it, which is where a fixture's canonical-output comparison has to live.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
          "assertions": [
            { "variable": "parentTotalAge", "time": 0.0, "expected": 820.0 }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
